{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "part 2 (last).", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/ad78b8c22ee14cd867434356cd2c876b7a09b8ddc5f781c03808bc33d2ed08ec.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.48], [2, 0.8, 1.06]]}, {"text": "Upwinds for DS Jobs", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/4cdbfc553ff7e17129866d6978250c8cd90338824d93f40588b17b1a657ca034.mp3"}, {"text": "Engineers can use AutoML to create models", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3885772f0fbe9a2c2c0b4d75a5382dbc04b8f5a643b37bbbdbe1a7a5243848fb.mp3"}, {"text": "I was chatting with my friend Gregory Azuolas about what it really takes to train an ML model at Google.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8f9c7d3274bdb88d1fdefce7efd79d330f86d7472b65f420d8085dbf5b89a0fe.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.14], [1, 0.14, 0.28], [2, 0.28, 0.56], [3, 0.56, 0.78], [4, 0.78, 0.94], [5, 0.94, 1.26], [6, 1.26, 1.5], [8, 2.06, 2.4], [9, 2.4, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 2.72], [11, 2.72, 2.96], [12, 2.96, 3.24], [13, 3.24, 3.48], [14, 3.48, 3.68], [15, 3.68, 3.9], [18, 4.24, 4.6], [19, 4.6, 4.9]]}, {"text": "The company has gone all-in on automating ML training—not just by streamlining data pipelines and automating code deployments, but by eliminating much of the manual effort traditionally required to build models.", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/bbe828f93c48ffadd1b038ccae8dfaffbf4b70b00b71c4c354d49bde75fbbe11.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.2], [1, 0.2, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 0.88], [5, 1.42, 1.7], [6, 1.7, 2.18], [7, 2.18, 2.56], [9, 3.7, 3.88], [10, 3.88, 4.04], [11, 4.04, 4.56], [12, 4.56, 4.84], [13, 4.84, 5.28], [14, 5.28, 5.74], [15, 5.74, 6.2], [16, 6.2, 6.56], [17, 6.56, 7.26], [18, 7.48, 7.64], [19, 7.64, 7.78], [20, 7.78, 8.16], [21, 8.16, 8.52], [22, 8.52, 8.68], [23, 8.68, 8.8], [24, 8.8, 9.1], [25, 9.1, 9.5], [26, 9.5, 10.02], [27, 10.02, 10.5], [28, 10.5, 10.74], [29, 10.74, 10.92], [30, 10.92, 11.32]]}, {"text": "Google’s AutoML infrastructure allows engineers with no background in machine learning or data science to train classifiers across a wide range of data types and scales.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/328846c415cdfbce8594ca3700908f50c870d5389ae800cc1e84d77ddd10b715.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.5], [1, 0.5, 1.04], [2, 1.04, 1.68], [3, 1.68, 2.2], [4, 2.2, 2.7], [5, 2.7, 3.0], [6, 3.0, 3.2], [7, 3.2, 3.64], [8, 3.64, 3.86], [9, 3.86, 4.1], [10, 4.1, 4.48], [11, 4.48, 4.74], [12, 4.74, 4.94], [13, 4.94, 5.38], [14, 5.38, 5.66], [15, 5.66, 5.92], [16, 5.92, 6.64], [17, 6.64, 6.98], [18, 6.98, 7.2], [19, 7.2, 7.44], [20, 7.44, 7.74], [21, 7.74, 7.84], [22, 7.84, 8.0], [23, 8.0, 8.38], [24, 8.38, 8.54], [25, 8.54, 8.88]]}, {"text": "This shift reduces the need for specialized ML engineers to fine-tune models manually.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/1bb9c024b43e52fd50b592dbba169de76f75d250b680de9e5dde97834fd4b5b1.mp3"}, {"text": "Gregory acknowledged that AutoML models might not be the most efficient in terms of power consumption or latency.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a49928ac4edfbcf57bf8b8b92ac719755092a3d116343cb4dc412f186cdb894c.mp3", "words": [[1, 0.34, 0.84], [2, 0.84, 1.18], [4, 1.54, 2.0], [5, 2.0, 2.24], [6, 2.24, 2.44], [7, 2.44, 2.62], [8, 2.62, 2.74], [9, 2.74, 2.92], [10, 2.92, 3.34], [11, 3.34, 3.58], [12, 3.58, 3.76], [13, 3.76, 3.96], [14, 3.96, 4.2], [15, 4.2, 4.64], [16, 4.64, 4.92], [17, 4.92, 5.22]]}, {"text": "But in his view, the real cost in ML isn’t inference—it’s model creation.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/87eec2e355758def8ec7dce8d10005161da2ca90831e861bfd2e5ef9e3676abc.mp3"}, {"text": "While companies will continue optimizing inference efficiency (see DeepSeek-R1), the number of jobs dedicated to this task is relatively small.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/932db56f94f4a29d2e7f6e78435b21660b9da43f5efcac1a14064abc4cb32c1d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.58], [2, 0.58, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 1.1], [4, 1.1, 1.64], [5, 1.64, 2.04], [6, 2.04, 2.68], [9, 4.28, 4.4], [10, 4.4, 4.62], [11, 4.62, 4.78], [12, 4.78, 4.96], [13, 4.96, 5.46], [14, 5.46, 5.7], [15, 5.7, 5.88], [16, 5.88, 6.16], [17, 6.16, 6.36], [18, 6.36, 6.72], [19, 6.72, 7.24]]}, {"text": "The bigger trend is clear: the barrier to training ML models is getting lower, and the role of traditional ML engineers is evolving fast.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/63a932d99aac1c7b4601d0486edacf17564e8d6ecc030092577aa76efde4ae2d.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [1, 0.22, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.78], [3, 0.78, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.32], [5, 1.82, 1.9], [6, 1.9, 2.24], [7, 2.24, 2.48], [8, 2.48, 2.78], [9, 2.78, 3.08], [10, 3.08, 3.48], [11, 3.48, 3.8], [12, 3.8, 4.0], [13, 4.0, 4.32], [14, 4.72, 4.92], [15, 4.92, 5.02], [16, 5.02, 5.2], [17, 5.2, 5.38], [18, 5.38, 5.82], [19, 5.82, 6.24], [20, 6.24, 6.7], [21, 6.7, 7.08], [22, 7.08, 7.48], [23, 7.48, 7.84]]}, {"text": "Engineers can user LLMs to replace models", "block": 6, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a30d0a08b27a94afe66e0de3b21d8c07134f71ea6fdc06e2dc973bbdcb63e8db.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.56], [1, 0.56, 0.78], [3, 1.0, 1.64], [4, 1.64, 1.84], [5, 1.84, 2.16], [6, 2.16, 2.62]]}, {"text": "If performance and cost isn’t super critical, engineers can just use an GPT-based model to perform their classification.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9259650e8763ade3820295dc163bc410ab1940571ce1a4c83e012ae1280e4b8f.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.12], [1, 0.12, 0.56], [2, 0.56, 0.82], [3, 0.82, 1.08], [4, 1.08, 1.58], [5, 1.58, 1.92], [6, 1.92, 2.38], [7, 2.84, 3.2], [8, 3.2, 3.44], [9, 3.44, 3.66], [10, 3.66, 4.0], [13, 4.94, 5.22], [14, 5.22, 5.44], [15, 5.44, 5.82], [16, 5.82, 6.02], [17, 6.02, 6.52]]}, {"text": "Before ChatGPT, custom classifiers must be trained and retrained as the business / regulations change.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/799732127d66d21196b3e0ff9fe8407035ce5364a76860109d8ffcd1702cdae0.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.4], [2, 1.86, 2.14], [3, 2.14, 2.82], [4, 2.82, 3.02], [5, 3.02, 3.22], [6, 3.22, 3.58], [7, 3.58, 3.8], [8, 3.8, 4.24], [9, 4.24, 4.54], [10, 4.54, 4.7], [11, 4.7, 5.02], [13, 5.4, 5.98], [14, 5.98, 6.46]]}, {"text": "But since ChatGPT can do everything and is ready to do everything, there is no need to spend weeks or months trying to design and train a custom model for each business cases.", "block": 7, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/3de65d95257b22a10f50093317d25f7b6493e64cce8b08c930d130548801afc3.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.46], [2, 0.46, 1.22], [3, 1.22, 1.42], [4, 1.42, 1.56], [5, 1.56, 1.98], [6, 1.98, 2.24], [7, 2.24, 2.38], [8, 2.38, 2.56], [9, 2.56, 2.74], [10, 2.74, 2.86], [11, 2.86, 3.34], [12, 3.74, 3.92], [13, 3.92, 4.08], [14, 4.08, 4.26], [15, 4.26, 4.44], [16, 4.44, 4.58], [17, 4.58, 4.84], [18, 4.84, 5.12], [19, 5.12, 5.46], [20, 5.46, 5.72], [21, 5.72, 6.0], [22, 6.0, 6.18], [23, 6.18, 6.5], [24, 6.5, 6.76], [25, 6.76, 7.02], [26, 7.02, 7.22], [27, 7.22, 7.52], [28, 7.52, 7.86], [29, 7.86, 8.12], [30, 8.12, 8.34], [31, 8.34, 8.64]]}, {"text": "Instead of a team of DS people outputting 1-2 models per month, 1 engineer can modify a prompt to chatgpt in days and now there is a now classification ready for production.", "block": 8, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5220c26e542fd8224214abe3ae3f84f1ee6da2861b32dccbb6e0666981807ebd.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.34], [1, 0.34, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.58], [3, 0.58, 0.78], [4, 0.78, 1.02], [5, 1.02, 1.24], [6, 1.24, 1.64], [7, 1.64, 2.14], [9, 2.54, 2.84], [10, 2.84, 3.04], [11, 3.04, 3.3], [13, 3.86, 4.36], [14, 4.36, 4.58], [15, 4.58, 4.92], [16, 4.92, 5.16], [17, 5.16, 5.4], [18, 5.4, 5.58], [20, 6.3, 6.54], [21, 6.54, 6.82], [22, 7.1, 7.24], [23, 7.24, 7.48], [24, 7.48, 7.68], [25, 7.68, 7.84], [26, 7.84, 7.9], [27, 7.9, 8.16], [28, 8.16, 8.72], [29, 8.72, 9.24], [30, 9.24, 9.46], [31, 9.46, 9.84]]}, {"text": "Once the AI has classified enough production data and inference costs (either dollar or latency) exceed budget, a custom model can easily be trained using automl by an engineer.", "block": 9, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/12f6f7581abf33faeffb60bfde12a0af08050c9162594c18e546154a6fe84ebb.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.28], [1, 0.28, 0.48], [2, 0.48, 0.72], [3, 0.72, 0.96], [4, 0.96, 1.36], [5, 1.36, 1.66], [6, 1.66, 2.06], [7, 2.06, 2.4], [9, 2.58, 2.88], [10, 2.88, 3.44], [11, 3.8, 3.96], [12, 3.96, 4.3], [13, 4.3, 4.54], [14, 4.54, 4.9], [15, 5.4, 5.68], [16, 5.68, 6.08], [17, 6.68, 6.8], [18, 6.8, 7.1], [19, 7.1, 7.44], [20, 7.44, 7.66], [21, 7.66, 8.0], [22, 8.0, 8.2], [23, 8.2, 8.48], [24, 8.48, 8.8], [27, 9.4, 9.54], [28, 9.54, 9.94]]}, {"text": "Data cleaning and generation", "block": 10, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/c946c3a8a7ba250e2f6ad523a63dd3bdbe279cc2eb13c869325749bc800ce72b.mp3"}, {"text": "Historically, data scientists spent a significant portion of their time collecting, labeling, and cleaning data—often writing complex scripts to sanitize and validate datasets before they were ready for model training.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/19c12c62547e6ecf482874b595087bbc9526f1cadfc80646435ca7054ff1320e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.76], [1, 0.94, 1.04], [2, 1.04, 1.52], [4, 1.84, 1.96], [5, 1.96, 2.42], [6, 2.42, 2.9], [7, 2.9, 3.08], [8, 3.08, 3.24], [9, 3.24, 3.5], [10, 3.5, 4.02], [11, 4.3, 4.6], [12, 4.94, 5.02], [13, 5.02, 5.3], [15, 6.28, 6.54], [16, 6.54, 7.02], [17, 7.02, 7.48], [18, 7.48, 7.8], [19, 7.8, 8.52], [20, 8.52, 8.72], [21, 8.72, 9.1], [23, 9.84, 10.16], [24, 10.16, 10.42], [25, 10.42, 10.56], [26, 10.56, 10.82], [27, 10.82, 11.04], [28, 11.04, 11.34], [29, 11.34, 11.76]]}, {"text": "But today, the bottleneck isn’t human effort; it’s inference time.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/9434cdc570bc52560ba6eab7d246264c5c4ecb19336303b473026c616179b02e.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.48], [2, 0.88, 0.96], [3, 0.96, 1.54], [4, 1.54, 1.84], [5, 1.84, 2.08], [6, 2.08, 2.44], [7, 2.92, 3.16], [9, 3.46, 3.82]]}, {"text": "Advances like DeepSeek and Stanford’s Alpaca have made major strides in leveraging inference for data generation and refinement.", "block": 11, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/e94c403e8f84c8323e6b6af9ab7ec9bbaeb2f087a9c03cce03e4cd49e84b00c8.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.56], [1, 0.56, 0.9], [3, 1.38, 1.6], [4, 1.6, 2.24], [5, 2.24, 2.7], [6, 2.7, 2.96], [7, 2.96, 3.12], [8, 3.12, 3.52], [9, 3.52, 4.0], [10, 4.0, 4.18], [11, 4.18, 4.52], [13, 5.2, 5.34], [14, 5.34, 5.56], [15, 5.56, 6.12], [16, 6.12, 6.46], [17, 6.46, 6.96]]}, {"text": "As a result, each data scientist can accomplish more with fewer resources, reducing the overall demand for headcount.", "block": 12, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/5c318193bd344736c95a3f5c6723b9b4c1dacde4eddae4a336fdeef3be4f1595.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.62], [3, 0.84, 1.02], [4, 1.02, 1.18], [5, 1.18, 1.74], [6, 1.74, 2.08], [7, 2.08, 2.5], [8, 2.5, 2.8], [9, 2.8, 3.02], [10, 3.02, 3.26], [11, 3.26, 3.88], [12, 4.32, 4.58], [13, 4.58, 4.84], [14, 4.84, 5.2], [15, 5.2, 5.48], [16, 5.48, 5.76], [17, 5.76, 6.12]]}, {"text": "[0] - Some people use the term “cheaper”, but I don’t think the talent should be considered cheap, b/c that has negative connotations of lower quality.", "block": 13, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a7e688d5ad71718e794217e139918d643bc94137c01825e1392c0239705b024e.mp3", "words": [[2, 1.02, 1.3], [3, 1.3, 1.6], [4, 1.6, 1.88], [5, 1.88, 2.02], [6, 2.02, 2.22], [8, 2.96, 3.24], [9, 3.24, 3.4], [10, 3.4, 3.56], [11, 3.56, 3.74], [12, 3.74, 3.92], [13, 3.92, 4.22], [14, 4.22, 4.46], [15, 4.46, 4.6], [16, 4.6, 5.0], [17, 5.0, 5.36], [18, 5.36, 5.86], [19, 5.86, 6.26], [20, 6.26, 6.42], [21, 6.42, 6.82], [22, 6.82, 7.58], [23, 7.58, 7.84], [24, 7.84, 8.14], [25, 8.14, 8.64]]}]}